---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const guide = {
  "title": "UAE Visit Visas for Pakistanis: Routes & Official Checks",
  "description": "Identify the UAE visit route, authorised submission channel and relevant authority before comparing prices or paying for a package.",
  "intro": "Identify the UAE visit route, authorised submission channel and relevant authority before comparing prices or paying for a package.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "UAE Government tourist visa guidance",
      "url": "https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/visa-and-emirates-id/residence-visas/tourist-visa"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dubai single-entry tourist service",
      "url": "https://www.gdrfad.gov.ae/en/services/f9e586fe-0642-11ec-0320-0050569629e8"
    },
    {
      "title": "UAE entry-permit checks",
      "url": "https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/visa-and-emirates-id/Visa-information/do-you-need-an-entry-permit-or-a-visa-to-enter-the-uae"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Match the route to the purpose",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Tourist visits, family visits, work and residence are different processes. The government describes a separate five-year multiple-entry tourist route, but its existence does not establish individual eligibility. Do not assume visit permission authorises taking a job."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Identify the issuing channel",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Dubai’s single-entry tourist service describes tourism-establishment sponsorship and 30- or 60-day options. It includes home-country identity evidence for some nationalities, including Pakistan. Check the actual service; one emirate’s procedure is not necessarily the rule for every UAE application."
      ],
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Request a written breakdown",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Ask an intermediary for the exact permit category, government charge, service fees, insurance, any deposit and cancellation conditions. Confirm who submits it and what happens after a document request or refusal.",
        "A commercial package name or a 24-hour claim does not establish the official category or outcome. Keep receipts and a traceable application reference; verify status through the responsible authority."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check current eligibility",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Confirm nationality, residence and evidence conditions with the issuing channel. Prepare the passport, identity, travel and host papers it requests. This guide does not make a blanket ban claim or promise approval for all Pakistani applicants."
      ],
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "heading": "Read the issued permit",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Check identity, last entry date, entries and authorised period. Have errors corrected by the issuer. Recheck before extending or changing status rather than assuming a package includes an extension. Keep accommodation, onward travel and emergency contacts accessible."
      ],
      "source": 0
    }
  ]
};
---
<GuideLayout {...guide} />
